{"_type":"issue","id":"local-agent-chat-599","title":"Research better document parsing than PDF.js (Docling, marker, unstructured, local OCR)","description":"Why: LibreChat's built-in document_parser (packages/api/src/files/documents/crud.ts, pdfToText) uses pdfjs-dist getTextContent and joins items with spaces per page. It loses layout, tables, headings and reading order in multi-column PDFs, and returns nothing for scanned pages (OCR needed). What: evaluate Docling (IBM, Python, layout+table aware, exposes a CLI/server), marker, unstructured and a local OCR option (tesseract/paddle) for quality vs cost on this machine (RTX 3060 12 GB shared with llama-server). Decide the integration seam: LibreChat already has pluggable extraction via fileConfig.ocr (strategy + supportedMimeTypes, see getUploadExtractedTextPlan in packages/api/src/protection/files.ts) and RAG_API_URL; a local HTTP service exposing an OCR-compatible or RAG-compatible interface would plug in without forking parser code. Output: a short spec under docs/superpowers/specs/ with the chosen tool, resource footprint, and the config to wire it. Depends on the PDF-to-text routing change (fileConfig override in librechat.yaml) being verified first.","status":"open","priority":3,"issue_type":"task","owner":"186934155+aquerman@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-10-03T07:21:24Z","created_by":"aquerman","updated_at":"2026-10-03T07:21:24Z","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"local-agent-chat-599","depends_on_id":"local-agent-chat-a56.2","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-10-03T07:23:35Z","created_by":"aquerman","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":1,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
